  by: agent  # 43c1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 43c1
  clock: 5  # 43c1
  nonce: 43c1  # 43c1
  message: "FIXED -- PR #733 (8955d9a22b, rebase-merged 2026-09-03 05:35Z). Status set to pending_validation, not satisfied: the item's\nstatement is about the CRON GATE delivering a move, and the closure evidence\nthis item names is \"a green self-claims-gate step on a subsequent firing,\nread via ci-debug cron-status\". That firing has not happened yet. What HAS\nbeen shown:\n\n1. THE MECHANISM, A/B'd ON THE SHIPPED PREDICATES. hypergumbo's own map\n   (105,931 Python call edges) replayed through _uncatalogued_external_modules\n   with the pre-fix and post-fix python.yaml: unknown modules 69 -> 68, the\n   single difference `builtins`, nothing added. 20,325 call edges name\n   `builtins` in the module slot -- INV-foluz's population -- and the\n   catalogue had no completeness entry for it.\n\n2. THE ITEM'S OWN REPRO, RE-RUN. The gate's own command\n   (`verify-claims . --claims docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml --json --minimal`,\n   then check-self-claims-drift against the snapshot) locally, before the\n   fix: the identical 40-line drift CI reported. After the fix: check-self-claims-drift reports OK, 18 claims unchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats) -- every verdict, caveat set and credited-flow bit back on the recorded snapshot, with no snapshot update.\n\n3. THE FIX IS A DECLARATION, NOT A GATE CHANGE. builtins is enumerated under\n   the survey's own rule; the new rows (print/breakpoint/copyright/credits ->\n   logging; license -> fs_read+logging; help -> logging+subprocess, unruled)\n   are the surfaces the rule required before the entry could be honest.\n   Survey addendum + tests against the SHIPPED catalogue.\n\n4. TWO CORRECTIONS THE SUITE MADE, NEITHER TOUCHING THE GATE. The six names\n   join ambiguous_names (builtins by construction; INV-mivud's derived rule\n   flagged them; hinted edges still match, hint-less bare calls are refused,\n   both pinned). builtins.help re-opens the unruled register INV-nular had\n   emptied -- neither settled ruling describes \"logging always, launch only\n   when the environment supplies a tty\" -- and WI-kapak owns that vocabulary\n   gap plus the disclosed-not-rowed no-argument stdin loop (ADR-0049).\n\nWHAT CLOSES IT: `ci-debug cron-status` showing `OK   self-claims-gate` on the\nfirst full-suite firing after merge (13:00 UTC), read back by whoever is in\nthe session then -- the per-step line exists now precisely so that this does\nnot need a log fetch."  # 43c1
