- op: discuss  # c124
  at: '2026-09-03T07:25:52Z'  # c124
  by: agent  # c124
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c124
  clock: 7  # c124
  nonce: c124  # c124
  message: "SATISFIED. The item's own named closure evidence, observed on the MERGED tree.\n`ci-debug cron-status`, run 2026-09-03 05:42Z:\n\n  OK   ci/woodpecker/cron/full-suite: success\n      OK   success  8955d9a2  2026-09-03T01:35:12-04:00  (1 commit(s) back)\n           https://ci.revolving-tactile.com.de/repos/1/pipeline/2206/1\n           OK   git / prepare-git / build-grammars / test-all-packages /\n                self-tree-validation / self-claims-gate / test-agent-infra\n\nPipeline 2206 is a full-suite run the owner triggered by hand right after\nPR #733 merged (8955d9a22b -- the fix commit itself). It posted under the\ncron context, on that commit, all seven steps OK, self-claims-gate among\nthem and readable beside its siblings without a log fetch -- which is what\nINV-bozid's per-step reader exists for. `ci-debug status 8955d9a2` agrees\n(push/woodpecker 9 steps OK; cron/full-suite 7 steps OK).\n\nWHY THIS OK IS NOT VACUOUS. scripts/check-self-claims exits 2 on any\ninfrastructure failure (hypergumbo_core not importable, no parseable JSON)\nand non-zero on any drift in either direction, so a green step means\ncheck-self-claims-drift returned 0: every verdict, caveat set and\ncredited-flow bit on the recorded snapshot -- the same \"OK, 18 claims\nunchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats)\" the fix produced locally with the\ngate's own command.\n\nCAVEAT, STATED. The step TRANSCRIPT was not read. `ci-debug logs\nself-claims-gate 8955d9a2` honestly reports \"nothing named\n'self-claims-gate' on this commit\" and shows push/woodpecker instead: the\nfetcher selects a gate by CONTEXT name and never searches a sibling\nstatus's pipeline for a STEP name, so it cannot fetch a step the per-step\nreader lists. Filed as WI-ratam (P2); the closure here rests on the\nconstruction argument above plus cron-status, not on the transcript.\n\nRegression window c2686a6131..4fcff62951 (five commits); red at the 09-02\n13:00Z and 09-03 01:00Z firings; green at pipeline 2206 on the fix.\nResiduals filed: WI-kapak (help's ruling vocabulary), WI-lujon (citation\ntests under smart-test), WI-ratam (logs step search)."  # c124
